{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:73f4a3f279861109","name":"Double Attack","source":{"id":"source:reference-73f4a3f279861109","title":"Double Attack","revision":24946,"timestamp":"2024-11-10T15:55:38Z","sha256":"f90da8d427c2fb2a1d9931e7ad3cce57eda645ea41e3fb19a78785fa9b5ba0c8","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24946","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Double%20Attack&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-73f4a3f279861109","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["You can make an additional attack during a round of combat.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Prerequisite:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Base Attack Bonus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus"}," +6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Effect:"]}," Choose a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapon"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Group"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Group"}," with which you are proficient. When you use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full_Attack"}," Action, you may make one additional attack when wielding such a weapon. However, you take a -5 penalty on all attack rolls until your next turn because you're trading precision for speed.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Normal:"]}," Making a single attack is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," You may select this Feat multiple times. Each time you select this Feat, it applies to a different ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapon"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Group"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Group"},". If you take this feat with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Weapons","referenceId":"reference:a2b1d4c4bac82300"},", it also applies with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Weapons"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Jedi Counseling"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Counseling"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Counseling"},")"]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Dual Weapon Mastery vs Double Attack"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Q:"]}," I'm curious as to the perceived balance factor of Dual Weapon Mastery versus Double Attack. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dual Weapon Mastery I"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dual_Weapon_Mastery_I","referenceId":"reference:f50ca7ec9196bfe9"}," is available sooner, and you can offset its penalties by taking more ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feats"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feats","referenceId":"reference:9194ccf56b9cace0"},". Double Attack works for only one type of weapon, and you can reduce its penalties only with Prestige Class ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"},". Since both grant an extra attack, why would you want Double Attack?\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["A:"]}," The balancing factor is that Dual Weapon Mastery works only with ",{"tag":"a","children":["One-Handed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/One-Handed"}," weapons (that is, weapons that do less damage), but Double Attack/",{"tag":"a","children":["Triple Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Triple_Attack","referenceId":"reference:a46348cb3be161eb"}," works with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Two-Handed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Two-Handed"}," weapons (but only one type of them). For example:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["A Dual Weapon Mastery specialist might use two ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Blaster Pistols"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Blaster_Pistols"},", which deal 3d8 points of damage per weapon, or a potential of 6d8 points from both."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["A Double Attack specialist might use a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Blaster Rifle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Blaster_Rifle","referenceId":"reference:40670bfa52c77cbd"},", which deals 3d10 points of damage but has a much better ",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"},". In addition, the weapon is capable of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Autofire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Autofire"},", so it can deal up to 5d10 points of damage with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst Fire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst_Fire","referenceId":"reference:ff3da4756d0ccd5c"},"."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["This also means that Double Attack can be used with much larger weapons, such as those on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},", while a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," would have no particular reason to use Dual Weapon Mastery because such weapons can't be operated with one hand.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Finally, don't forget that someone can use both Dual Weapon Mastery and Double Attack/",{"tag":"a","children":["Triple Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Triple_Attack","referenceId":"reference:a46348cb3be161eb"},". So even if Dual Weapon Mastery appears more attractive at first, you might want to take Double Attack/",{"tag":"a","children":["Triple Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Triple_Attack","referenceId":"reference:a46348cb3be161eb"}," later.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Multiple Attacks with Multiple Targets"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Q:"]}," Can you use Double Attack or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Triple Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Triple_Attack","referenceId":"reference:a46348cb3be161eb"}," to attack the same target multiple times in the same round, or do you have to attack different targets?\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["A:"]}," The extra attacks from Double Attack, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Triple Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Triple_Attack","referenceId":"reference:a46348cb3be161eb"},", and fighting with multiple weapons can be directed at the same target or at different targets, in any combination and any order that you choose.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Double and Rapid Attacks"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Q:"]}," It is possible to use Double Attack with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rapid Strike"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rapid_Strike","referenceId":"reference:700a0453398913da"},"?\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["A:"]}," Yes. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rapid Strike"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rapid_Strike","referenceId":"reference:700a0453398913da"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rapid Shot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rapid_Shot","referenceId":"reference:d5cac053fa8ba463"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst Fire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst_Fire","referenceId":"reference:ff3da4756d0ccd5c"}," all can be used when making multiple attacks, regardless of their source (Double Attack, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Triple Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Triple_Attack","referenceId":"reference:a46348cb3be161eb"},", or fighting with multiple weapons).\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
